/-!
# The rank of the conormal sheaf and the number of equations cutting out an immersion

Let `i : Z ⟶ S` be an immersion into a locally Noetherian scheme and let `z : Z`.  Write
`𝔞 = RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom` for the ideal of the local ring `𝒪_{S, i z}` cutting out
`Z` at `z`.  This file identifies the rank of the conormal sheaf of `i` with the minimal number
of generators of `𝔞`, in both directions, and expresses that number as the dimension of the
cotangent fibre `𝔞 / 𝔪 𝔞` over the residue field.

The rank is not part of the data of a regular immersion:  regularity only asks that each `𝔞` be
generated by *some* regular sequence.  Fixing the length of that sequence, uniformly in `z`, is
exactly fixing the rank of the conormal sheaf.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_eq_of_basis_conormalStalk`:  the engine.  A basis
  of the stalk at `z` of the conormal sheaf, read as a basis of the cotangent module of the
  kernel of the coborder stalk map, has cardinality the minimal number of generators of `𝔞`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_universalConormalSheaf_of_stalk_span`:  **the rank
  from the generators.**  If every `𝔞` is generated by a weakly regular sequence of length `n`,
  the conormal sheaf of `i` is finite locally free of rank `n`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_eq_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.finrank_cotangentFibre_ker_stalkMap_eq_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank`:  **the
  generators from the rank.**  If the conormal sheaf of `i` is finite locally free of rank `n`,
  then `𝔞` needs exactly `n` generators, equivalently its cotangent fibre `𝔞 / 𝔪 𝔞` has
  dimension `n` over the residue field.  Any `n` generators of `𝔞` are therefore minimal.

## Implementation notes

The stalk of the conormal sheaf of `i` at `z` is the cotangent module `I / I²` of the kernel `I`
of the surjection `𝒪_{coborder, i z} ⟶ 𝒪_{Z,z}` of local rings, by
`Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheafStalkEquivCotangent`, and that kernel corresponds to `𝔞` under the
stalk isomorphism of the open immersion `i.coborderRange.ι`.  So a free presentation of the
conormal stalk is a free presentation of `I / I²` over `𝒪_{Z,z}`, hence — after transporting the
coefficients along `𝒪_{Z,z} ≅ 𝒪_{coborder, i z} / I` — over that quotient ring, where
`Ideal.spanFinrank_top_cotangent_eq_spanFinrank` converts the rank of `I / I²` into the minimal
number of generators of `I`.  That number is invariant under a ring isomorphism, which carries it
back to `𝔞`.  No tensor computation and no comparison of two residue fields is needed anywhere;
the whole bridge is the minimal-number-of-generators function.

Both main statements are local on `Z`, and the rank is read pointwise through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.fiberRank`.  For the direction *from* the generators the input
is the stalkwise criterion for Tag 063I,
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isRegularImmersion_of_exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap`,
which turns the pointwise hypothesis into regularity of the immersion;  Tag 063K then makes it
quasi-regular and Tag 063M makes the conormal sheaf finite locally free, after which
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_restrict_of_fiberRank_eq` upgrades
finite local freeness to finite local freeness of rank `n`.  The hypothesis is stated with
`RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular`, the weaker of the two notions:  a stalk ideal of an
immersion is proper, so it lies in the maximal ideal and
`IsLocalRing.isRegular_iff_isWeaklyRegular_of_subset_maximalIdeal` recovers regularity.

The residue field is spelled as the quotient `𝒪_{S, i z} ⧸ 𝔪` rather than as
`IsLocalRing.ResidueField`, because the latter is a plain definition and the module structure on
the cotangent fibre is not found for it by instance search.  The two are definitionally equal.

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Lemma 31.22.5 (063M)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063M)
* [The Stacks Project, Lemma 31.21.3 (063I)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063I)
* [The Stacks Project, Lemma 31.21.2 (063K)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063K)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf
open Stacks.Thickenings (universalConormalSheaf)

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

attribute [local instance] Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheafStalkModule
  Stacks.Conormal.stalkMapAlgebra Stacks.Conormal.cotangentStalkModule

/-- **The rank of the conormal stalk is the minimal number of generators of the stalk ideal.**
If the cotangent module `I / I²` of the kernel `I` of the stalk map of the canonical closed
factor of an immersion `i : Z ⟶ S` into a locally Noetherian scheme has a basis indexed by
`Fin r` over `𝒪_{Z,z}`, then the ideal `RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom` of `𝒪_{S, i z}` needs
exactly `r` generators.

The basis is transported to the quotient ring `𝒪_{coborder, i z} / I`, which is isomorphic to
`𝒪_{Z,z}` and over which `I / I²` is therefore free of rank `r`;  the minimal number of
generators of `I / I²` is the minimal number of generators of `I`, and the stalk isomorphism of
the open immersion `i.coborderRange.ι` carries `I` to the stalk ideal of `i`. -/
theorem spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_eq_of_basis_conormalStalk {Z S : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ S)
    [IsImmersion i] [IsLocallyNoetherian S] {r : ℕ} (z : Z)
    (b : Module.Basis (Fin r) (ToType (Z.presheaf.stalk z))
      (RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom).Cotangent) :
    (RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom).spanFinrank = r := by
  have hne : RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom ≠ ⊤ := RingHom.ker_ne_top _
  have hnt : Nontrivial (ToType (i.coborderRange.toScheme.presheaf.stalk
      (i.liftCoborder.base z)) ⧸ RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom) :=
    Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr hne
  let b' := b.mapCoeffs (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective
    (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap_surjective z)).symm fun _ _ => rfl
  have hfree : Module.Free (ToType (i.coborderRange.toScheme.presheaf.stalk
      (i.liftCoborder.base z)) ⧸ RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom)
      (RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom).Cotangent := Module.Free.of_basis b'
  have hfr : Module.finrank (ToType (i.coborderRange.toScheme.presheaf.stalk
      (i.liftCoborder.base z)) ⧸ RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom)
      (RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom).Cotangent = r := by
    simpa using Module.finrank_eq_card_basis b'
  have hsf : (RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom).spanFinrank = r := by
    rw [← Ideal.spanFinrank_top_cotangent_eq_spanFinrank _ hne,
      ← Module.finrank_eq_spanFinrank_of_free, hfr]
  have hfac : i = i.liftCoborder ≫ i.coborderRange.ι := i.liftCoborder_ι.symm
  let e : S.presheaf.stalk (i z) ≃+*
      i.coborderRange.toScheme.presheaf.stalk (i.liftCoborder.base z) :=
    (S.presheaf.stalkCongr
      (.of_eq (congrArg (fun q : Z ⟶ S => q z) hfac))).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.trans
      (asIso (i.coborderRange.ι.stalkMap (i.liftCoborder.base z))).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv
  have hmap : (i.stalkMap z).hom = (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom.comp e.toRingHom := by
    conv_lhs => rw [Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_congr_hom i (i.liftCoborder ≫ i.coborderRange.ι) hfac z]
    rw [Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_comp]
    rfl
  have hker : RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom =
      Ideal.map e.symm (RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom) := by
    rw [hmap, ← RingHom.comap_ker, Ideal.map_symm]
    rfl
  rw [hker, Ideal.spanFinrank_map_eq_of_ringEquiv, hsf]

/-! ### The generators from the rank -/

/-- **An immersion whose conormal sheaf has rank `n` needs exactly `n` equations in every local
ring.**  The upper bound is `AlgebraicGeometry.spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_le_of_conormal_rank`;  what
is added here is the lower bound, which comes from the stalk of the conormal sheaf being free of
rank exactly `n` rather than merely generated by `n` elements. -/
theorem spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_eq_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank {Z S : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ S)
    [IsImmersion i] [IsLocallyNoetherian S] (n : ℕ)
    (h : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) n)
    (z : Z) : (RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom).spanFinrank = n := by
  obtain ⟨b⟩ : Nonempty (Module.Basis (Fin n) (ToType (Z.presheaf.stalk z))
      (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
        (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i).val.presheaf z))) :=
    nonempty_basis_stalk_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) n h z
  exact spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_eq_of_basis_conormalStalk i z
    (b.map (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheafStalkEquivCotangent i z))

/-- **The cotangent fibre of the stalk ideal has dimension the rank of the conormal sheaf.**
For an immersion `i : Z ⟶ S` into a locally Noetherian scheme whose conormal sheaf is finite
locally free of rank `n`, the fibre `𝔞 / 𝔪 𝔞` of the ideal `𝔞 = RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom`
is an `n`-dimensional vector space over the residue field `𝒪_{S, i z} ⧸ 𝔪`.

Consequently any family of `n` elements generating `𝔞` is a minimal generating family:  their
classes span an `n`-dimensional space, so they are linearly independent over the residue
field. -/
theorem finrank_cotangentFibre_ker_stalkMap_eq_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank {Z S : Scheme.{u}}
    (i : Z ⟶ S) [IsImmersion i] [IsLocallyNoetherian S] (n : ℕ)
    (h : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) n)
    (z : Z) :
    Module.finrank (ToType (S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z)) ⧸
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (ToType (S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z))))
      (RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom ⧸
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (ToType (S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z))) •
          (⊤ : Submodule (ToType (S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z)))
            (RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom))) = n := by
  rw [← IsLocalRing.spanFinrank_eq_finrank_quotient _ (IsNoetherian.noetherian _)]
  exact spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_eq_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank i n h z

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_eq_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank` stated for the
universal conormal sheaf of Stacks 04F4. -/
theorem spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_eq_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_universalConormalSheaf
    {Z S : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ S) [IsImmersion i] [IsLocallyNoetherian S] (n : ℕ)
    (h : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} (universalConormalSheaf i) n)
    (z : Z) : (RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom).spanFinrank = n :=
  spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_eq_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank i n
    (SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.of_iso.{u, u, u}
      (Stacks.Thickenings.immersionConormalSheafIsoUniversalConormalSheaf i).symm h) z

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.finrank_cotangentFibre_ker_stalkMap_eq_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank` stated
for the universal conormal sheaf of Stacks 04F4. -/
theorem finrank_cotangentFibre_ker_stalkMap_eq_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_universalConormalSheaf
    {Z S : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ S) [IsImmersion i] [IsLocallyNoetherian S] (n : ℕ)
    (h : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} (universalConormalSheaf i) n)
    (z : Z) :
    Module.finrank (ToType (S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z)) ⧸
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (ToType (S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z))))
      (RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom ⧸
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (ToType (S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z))) •
          (⊤ : Submodule (ToType (S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z)))
            (RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom))) = n :=
  finrank_cotangentFibre_ker_stalkMap_eq_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank i n
    (SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.of_iso.{u, u, u}
      (Stacks.Thickenings.immersionConormalSheafIsoUniversalConormalSheaf i).symm h) z

/-! ### The rank from the generators -/

/-- The pointwise hypothesis of
`AlgebraicGeometry.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_universalConormalSheaf_of_stalk_span` makes the
immersion quasi-regular, and pins the minimal number of generators of every stalk ideal to
`n`. -/
private theorem spanFinrank_eq_and_isQuasiRegularImmersion_of_stalk_span {Z S : Scheme.{u}}
    (i : Z ⟶ S) [IsImmersion i] [IsLocallyNoetherian S] (n : ℕ)
    (h : ∀ z : Z, ∃ g : Fin n → S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z),
      RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular (ToType (S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z))) (List.ofFn g) ∧
        RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom = Ideal.span (Set.range g)) :
    (∀ z : Z, (RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom).spanFinrank = n) ∧
      IsQuasiRegularImmersion i := by
  have key : ∀ z : Z, ∃ rs : List (ToType (S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z))),
      RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular (ToType (S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z))) rs ∧
        Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom ∧ rs.length = n := by
    intro z
    obtain ⟨g, hwreg, hspan⟩ := h z
    have hset : {r | r ∈ List.ofFn g} = Set.range g := by ext x; simp
    have hofList : Ideal.ofList (List.ofFn g) = RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom := by
      rw [Ideal.ofList, hset, hspan]
    have hne : RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom ≠ ⊤ := RingHom.ker_ne_top _
    have hmem : ∀ r ∈ List.ofFn g, r ∈
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (ToType (S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z))) := fun r hr =>
      IsLocalRing.le_maximalIdeal hne (hofList ▸ Ideal.subset_span hr)
    exact ⟨List.ofFn g,
      (IsLocalRing.isRegular_iff_isWeaklyRegular_of_subset_maximalIdeal hmem).mpr hwreg,
      hofList, List.length_ofFn⟩
  refine ⟨fun z => ?_, ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨rs, hreg, hofList, hlen⟩ := key z
    rw [← hofList, Koszul.spanFinrank_eq_length_of_isRegular rs hreg, hlen]
  · refine isQuasiRegularImmersion_of_isH1RegularImmersion i
      (isH1RegularImmersion_of_isKoszulRegularImmersion i
        (isKoszulRegularImmersion_of_isRegularImmersion i ?_))
    refine isRegularImmersion_of_exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap i fun z => ?_
    obtain ⟨rs, hreg, hofList, -⟩ := key z
    exact ⟨rs, hreg, hofList⟩

/-- The fibre rank of a finite locally free conormal sheaf at `z` is the minimal number of
generators of the stalk ideal at `z`:  the stalk is free, so its fibre rank is its rank over the
local ring, and that rank is read by
`AlgebraicGeometry.spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_eq_of_basis_conormalStalk`. -/
private theorem fiberRank_conormalSheaf_eq_spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap {Z S : Scheme.{u}}
    (i : Z ⟶ S) [IsImmersion i] [IsLocallyNoetherian S]
    (hflf : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i))
    (z : Z) :
    Scheme.Modules.fiberRank (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) z =
      (RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom).spanFinrank := by
  have hflf' : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree (R := Z.ringCatSheaf)
      (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) := hflf
  have hft := Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherenceCriteria.isFiniteType_of_isFiniteLocallyFree
    (R := Z.ringCatSheaf) (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i)
  have hff := Stacks.StalkFreeBridge.freeAndFinite_stalk_of_isFiniteLocallyFree
    (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) z
  have hfree : Module.Free (ToType (Z.presheaf.stalk z))
      (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
        (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i).val.presheaf z)) := hff.1
  have hfin : Module.Finite (ToType (Z.presheaf.stalk z))
      (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
        (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i).val.presheaf z)) := hff.2
  have hgoal : Module.finrank (ToType (Z.presheaf.stalk z))
      (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
        (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i).val.presheaf z)) =
      (RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom).spanFinrank := by
    have b := (Module.Free.chooseBasis (ToType (Z.presheaf.stalk z))
      (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
        (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i).val.presheaf z))).reindex (Fintype.equivFin _)
    rw [Module.finrank_eq_card_chooseBasisIndex]
    exact (spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap_eq_of_basis_conormalStalk i z
      (b.map (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheafStalkEquivCotangent i z))).symm
  rw [Scheme.Modules.fiberRank_eq_finrank_stalk (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) z hff.1]
  exact hgoal

/-- **Stacks 063M with the rank.**  The conormal sheaf of an immersion into a locally Noetherian
scheme whose stalk ideals are all generated by weakly regular sequences of length `n` is finite
locally free of rank `n`.

The hypothesis makes the immersion regular (Tag 063I), hence quasi-regular (Tag 063K), hence its
conormal sheaf finite locally free (Tag 063M);  the fibre rank is then `n` at every point because
the minimal number of generators of every stalk ideal is `n`. -/
theorem isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_conormalSheaf_of_stalk_span {Z S : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ S)
    [IsImmersion i] [IsLocallyNoetherian S] (n : ℕ)
    (h : ∀ z : Z, ∃ g : Fin n → S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z),
      RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular (ToType (S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z))) (List.ofFn g) ∧
        RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom = Ideal.span (Set.range g)) :
    SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) n := by
  obtain ⟨hsf, hQ⟩ := spanFinrank_eq_and_isQuasiRegularImmersion_of_stalk_span i n h
  have hflf : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) :=
    isFiniteLocallyFree_conormalSheaf_of_isQuasiRegularImmersion i hQ
  have hfib : ∀ x : Z, x ∈ (⊤ : Z.Opens) →
      Scheme.Modules.fiberRank (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) x = n := fun x _ =>
    (fiberRank_conormalSheaf_eq_spanFinrank_ker_stalkMap i hflf x).trans (hsf x)
  have hflf' : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree (R := Z.ringCatSheaf)
    (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) := hflf
  have hres := Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_restrict_of_fiberRank_eq
    (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) ⊤ n hfib
  exact (Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_iff (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) n).mp <|
    Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_of_iSup_eq_top (fun _ : Unit => (⊤ : Z.Opens))
    (by simp) fun _ => Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_of_sheafOfModules _ n hres

/-- **Stacks 063M with the rank, for the universal conormal sheaf of Stacks 04F4.**  If every
stalk ideal `RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom` of an immersion `i : Z ⟶ S` into a locally
Noetherian scheme is generated by a weakly regular sequence of length `n`, then the conormal
sheaf of `i` is finite locally free of rank `n`. -/
theorem isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_universalConormalSheaf_of_stalk_span {Z S : Scheme.{u}}
    (i : Z ⟶ S) [IsImmersion i] [IsLocallyNoetherian S] (n : ℕ)
    (h : ∀ z : Z, ∃ g : Fin n → S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z),
      RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular (ToType (S.presheaf.stalk (i.base z))) (List.ofFn g) ∧
        RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom = Ideal.span (Set.range g)) :
    SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} (universalConormalSheaf i) n :=
  SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.of_iso.{u, u, u}
    (Stacks.Thickenings.immersionConormalSheafIsoUniversalConormalSheaf i)
    (isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_conormalSheaf_of_stalk_span i n h)

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
